	<item>
		<title>By: Lewis Cannon</title>
		<link>http://fffff.at/ai-weiwei-released/comment-page-1/#comment-31792</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Lewis Cannon]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 23 Jun 2011 15:44:48 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://fffff.at/?p=6926#comment-31792</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Ai is out (22/6) but no one should kid themselves that his release represents any softening of the Chinese approach towards dissent. Beijing remains as hardline as ever on freedom of expression and, if anything, it&#039;s getting harder, not softer. If you&#039;ve any doubt I suggest you read the excellent and hugely entertaining book &#039;Limp Pigs and the Five-Ring Circus&#039; by Mark Newham, a British journalist who penetrated to the heart of China&#039;s propaganda machine and survived to tell a previously untold tale. Highly recommended to anyone who cares about such things. China changing? Pah.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Ai is out (22/6) but no one should kid themselves that his release represents any softening of the Chinese approach towards dissent. Beijing remains as hardline as ever on freedom of expression and, if anything, it&#8217;s getting harder, not softer. If you&#8217;ve any doubt I suggest you read the excellent and hugely entertaining book &#8216;Limp Pigs and the Five-Ring Circus&#8217; by Mark Newham, a British journalist who penetrated to the heart of China&#8217;s propaganda machine and survived to tell a previously untold tale. Highly recommended to anyone who cares about such things. China changing? Pah.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
